# This repo's whole runtime target is Linux/macOS JVM processes and Linux containers (see
# CLAUDE.md's own node-topology section); a text file checked out with Windows CRLF line endings
# and then executed as a POSIX shell script inside a Linux container fails outright (dash's own
# "set -eu" parses a trailing \r as an illegal option character). Normalizing every text file to LF
# on checkout, regardless of a contributor's own local core.autocrlf setting, avoids that class of
# bug entirely rather than requiring every shipped shell script to defend against it individually.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit even though the blanket rule above already covers extensioned scripts: these are the
# ones actually executed with /bin/sh inside a container (gimle-holmgang/compose/*.sh) or bundled
# straight into a shipped archive and run on an operator's own machine (gimle-dist's own launcher
# scripts, which have no file extension at all so text=auto's own content-sniffing is the only thing
# that would otherwise catch them).
*.sh text eol=lf
gimle-dist/src/main/dist/bin/* text eol=lf
